        <div class="research-entry-details">
          <p>
            <strong>Description:</strong>{" "}
            Plant health management requires continuous context rather than
            isolated sensor readings. PlantLife365 connects an ESP32
            multisensor node with an authenticated Django platform to collect
            temperature, humidity, soil-moisture, light, gas, and optional
            image data. The platform organizes these measurements into live
            conditions, historical trends, configurable alerts, rolling
            statistics, and exportable user-owned records.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Outcome:</strong>{" "}
            The project translates multimodal sensing into an operational
            decision-support workflow spanning edge acquisition, secure
            ingestion, user-scoped data services, browser-based monitoring,
            exploratory regression analytics, and an optional local AI
            assistant.
          </p>

          <p class="research-entry-support">
            <strong>Project support:</strong>{" "}
            Mississippi Institutions of Higher Learning
          </p>
